WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:05.390
Let's get something clear right off the bat:
Big, hammy acting isn't necessarily a bad

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:05.880
thing.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.540
Subtlety and realism have their place, but
so do grand gestures, wild screaming, and

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.120
jumping up and down like a madman.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.100
Sometimes, overblown acting blends in perfectly
with the zaniness of the film, and sometimes

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.160
it works as a brilliant juxtaposition to all
the serious stuff happening on-screen.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.840
These are some of the greatest over-the-top
film performances of all time.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.800
The final frontier

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.360
If you're a fan of exaggerated acting, it
doesn't get any better than Star Trek II:

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.320
The Wrath of Khan.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.140
On one side of the aisle, you've got William
Shatner as Admiral James T. Kirk, and on the

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.360
other hand you have:

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.780
"KHAAAAAAAN.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.740
KHAAAAAAN."

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.960
And speaking of Khan, the award for deliciously
hammy acting goes to Ricardo Montalban for

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.540
playing the genetically engineered Übermensch
. With perfect pecs and a twinkle in his eye,

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.180
Montalban is having a blast as Kirk's arch-enemy.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.280
Whether he's making death threats or giving
romantic speeches, the man literally hisses

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.040
with hatred.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.440
"Ahhhhh…

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.240
Not so wounded as we were led to believe.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.900
So much the better."

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.280
It's even more fun in the scenes where he's
playing against Shatner; with all their exaggerated

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.740
gestures, it feels like an unstoppable force
meeting an immovable object.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.180
"Kirk… you're still alive, my old friend."

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.120
"Still.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:23.340
Old.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.320
Friend."

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:29.820
It's a true space opera, and Montalban knows
exactly what he's doing: boldly going where

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.920
no Star Trek villain had gone before.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.900
Say hello to my little friend

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.760
Directed by Brian De Palma, Scarface is one
of the greatest gangster movies ever made,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.140
and that's thanks to Al Pacino's performance
as Tony Montana.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.219
With an outrageous accent, Pacino bullies
his way through every scene, dripping with

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.980
venom as he drops epic lines:

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.260
"Why don't you try sticking your head up your
a--.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.540
See if it fits."

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.109
The more cocaine he snorts, the crazier his
performance becomes, and Pacino is absolutely

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:03.080
mesmerizing as he staggers through a restaurant,
telling the patrons

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.540
"So say goodnight to the bad guy.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.240
Come on."

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.800
Of course, his tour de force moment comes
in the film's climax, as the drug-addled kingpin

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.460
grabs a machine gun and utters his most iconic
line:

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.740
"Say hello to my little friend."

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.060
It's an incredible scene, big and bloody and
unbelievably bonkers, just like Pacino's performance.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.820
Game over, man!

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.959
The first four Alien films were all anchored
by Sigourney Weaver's lean, mean, and fantastic

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.060
turn as Ellen Ripley.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.840
But while Weaver plays a strong, spartan hero,
Bill Paxton takes things in a slightly more

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.160
eccentric direction in the second film Aliens.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.260
As Private Hudson, Paxton plays the ultimate
dude bro who think he's the ultimate badass.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.340
Hudson has a big, dumb grin, a cocksure swagger,
and he walks around like a John Wayne wannabe.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.000
If there was an Oscar for obnoxiousness, Paxton
would've picked up the prize.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.780
"Is this gonna be a stand-up fight, sir, or
just another bug hunt?"

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.749
But when the xenomorphs show up, all that
frat boy bravado scurries away, leaving a

00:03:01.749 --> 00:03:04.020
wide-eyed Hudson in permanent freak-out mode.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.080
It's not a game to Hudson anymore.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:06.720
In fact:

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.880
"well, that's it man, game over man.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:10.880
GAME OVER."

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.020
Hail to the king, baby

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.900
While Bruce Campbell's performance as the
unfortunate Ash Williams was pitch perfect

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.600
in the first two Evil Dead movies, Army of
Darkness lets the man go absolutely wild.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:25.360
There's nothing holding him back here, and
Campbell is having the time of his life dropping

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.240
one-liners that are oozing with cheese.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.040
"Alright you primitive screwheads, listen up.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.360
See this?

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.620
This... is my BOOMSTICK."

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.760
When he fights a witch in a watery pit, Campbell
plays the part like a WWE star.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.980
And when skeletal arms start popping out of
a cemetery, his little dance through the graveyard

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.320
is downright delightful.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.480
The greatest showcase of his unique talents
comes when he battles an army of pint-sized

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.140
Ash monsters and sings "London Bridge is Falling
Down."

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:01.260
"London bridge is falling down, falling down.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.960
Falling down."

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.240
It's an incredibly bizarre sequence think
Jim Carrey meets the Three Stooges.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:13.820
It's wonderful, schlocky fun, and when it
comes to over-the-top performances, well:

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.520
"Hail to the king, baby."

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.800
Thanks for watching!

